Per-MIME clipboard reads, writes and listings for the Kitty clipboard protocol (OSC 5522).

GPUI's ClipboardItem carries text, images and paths only. `write_clipboard_representations`
owns the clipboard or primary selection with exactly the given representations (Ghostty
83fb956, GTK surface.zig `set`: one provider per MIME, `text/plain` offered as
`text/plain;charset=utf-8` first); none gives the selection up. `read_clipboard_mimes`
reads each requested type the owner offers, a text type from its best text target, and
`clipboard_mime_types` lists the advertised MIME types without reading data. The
functions reach the registered LinuxPlatform on the main thread and report Unsupported
while headless or without a primary selection. Wayland and X11 both serve their own
selection from the stored representations. Wayland rejects NUL-containing MIME names
before replacing either selection or advertising them, and reads stored text aliases
through the same source selection and conversion as foreign offers. X11 updates the
cached item only after a successful write, and refuses writes larger than its native
single-request payload limit before changing the selection; outgoing INCR is not yet
implemented. An individual request failure is refused without stopping the worker.

